notes: 'Imported from mim-queue (source_id=mediadive.ingredient:471); no CAS-RN or
  CHEBI/NCIT match. Curated to NCIT:C29298 Oatmeal Powder on 2026-05-11.


  #1201 isolated proposal: Record the explicitly powdered Quaker White Oats input
  from JCM 52/NBRC 304 in supplied_form, without creating a second brand owner or
  adding global aliases. This physical form is not automatically the fine colloidal
  whole-oat form in NCITC29298. MediaDive 471/DSMZ 425 generic food oatmeal is not
  automatically powdered. Existing whole-owner mapping is retained under an explicit
  unresolved identity hold, rather than silently regrounded from three cases. Current
  23 matching source rows and full recipe bytes plus 18 historical candidate readbacks
  were inspected; exact membership of the old 18-count untracked table is not established.
  The old 18-member occurrence table at CultureMech 15a 4da 5c 08 is absent from git;
  current 23 rows include 18 MediaRecipes and 5 SolutionRecipes. Exact historical
  membership and fine/colloidal form scope require reconciliation before whole-owner
  reidentification. This does not block adding the supported source-stated supplied
  form. Raw source spellings are retained in case evidence and this source scope;
  no new globally resolving source-local alias is added. Full-owner publication approval
  and all source-specific holds remain pending.


  Final-review identity correction (#1232): the active exact NCIT:C29298 claim is
  withdrawn because its colloidal whole-oat fine-powder definition is not established
  by generic food oatmeal or merely powdered Quaker inputs. The existing food-oatmeal
  owner is represented by kgmicrobe.ingredient:oatmeal, with NARROW_MATCH to FOODON:00001189
  oat food product (a food product made from oats). This is an asymmetric broader
  food-material grounding, not exact identity with all oat foods and not a new brand
  or colloidal-grade owner. The prior identifier and exact mapping remain in immutable
  before bytes and the historical events below; earlier notes describing the retained
  NCIT hold are historical and superseded by this correction. All30 matching historical
  normalized recipe contexts at CultureMech15a4da5c08 were inspected in addition to
  the prior current-source lineage; their oatmeal inputs do not establish colloidal
  manufacture. The absent untracked18-member table is not claimed reconstructed; occurrence
  counts remain unchanged pending reconciliation. Powdered Quaker supplied-form facts
  remain source-specific; generic MediaDive471 oatmeal is not declared powdered. Whole-owner
  integration/export approval, unresolved occurrence membership and source-specific
  holds remain.'
ingredient_type: UNDEFINED_MIXTURE
supplied_form:
- name: Quaker White Oats (powdered)
  form: powder, as stated by JCM52 and NBRC304
  supplier: Quaker
  notes: 'JCM52 Oatmeal-Nitrate Agar and NBRC304 specify3g powdered Quaker White Oats
    as input. No catalog, grain-size limit, colloidal manufacture or NCITC29298 exact
    identity is inferred. This source-form addition does not establish powder processing
    for generic MediaDive471 oatmeal. Sources: https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=52
    ; https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=304'
